      \field{abstract}{The development of artificial intelligence (AI) in the beauty industry can reshape the way consumers interact with businesses, enabling them to quickly select more suitable products and providing a more convenient, targeted, and safer comfortable experience. Cosmetics companies integrate AI technology with offline shopping models, not only enhancing customer engagement and novelty in the store but also allowing businesses to identify products that customers prefer and target. South Korea is the first country in the world to enact laws and policies related to the customized cosmetics industry. South Korea's use of AI technology to develop customized cosmetics has been widely noticed in the international beauty market. The AI technology-based customized cosmetics industry in South Korea is mainly composed of three major industries: cosmetic products (skin care, makeup, beauty and hair care, and related products), beauty devices, and software services. In 2015, after Amorepacific Group first developed customized cosmetics in South Korea, companies such as LG Household \&amp; Health Care Ltd, CJ On Style, and H&amp;B began to engage in research and development in the customized cosmetics industry, achieving good results in both technology and product development. This study collects and investigates the development strategies of South Korean customized cosmetics companies and analyzes and organizes the methods of use and production principles of related products. It is hoped to provide some reference value for the development strategies and product research and development of global AI customized cosmetics companies.}
